# Dweller — Project Brief

## What this is

A home health report app. Someone enters a UK postcode and gets back a report scoring their home on water quality, air quality, structural health, noise, and local environmental risk, each rated green/orange/red.

## Repo structure

- `/frontend` — James's app, built in Claude Design, handed off into this folder.
- `/backend` — the database and API logic, described below.

## Data tables

| Table name | What it holds |
|---|---|
| `postcode_spine` | Every UK postcode with its map location, everything else references this. |
| `water_companies` | ~20 rows of manually researched water company data: hardness, nitrate, lead, THMs, chlorine, pH, compliance %, PFAS notice. |
| `postcode_to_water_company` | Lookup: postcode prefix -> which water company. |
| `hardness_geology_estimate` | Our own more granular hardness model, built from geology data, cross-checked against `water_companies`. |
| `air_quality_grid` | PM2.5 and NO2 by area, from the government's national grid file. |
| `radon_grid` | Radon risk class (1-6) by area. |
| `noise_grid` | Night-time road and rail noise by area. |
| `light_pollution_grid` | Light pollution estimate from satellite data. |
| `green_space` | Distance to nearest park/green space. |
| `historic_landfill` | Whether a postcode is near a former landfill. Personal details from the source data stripped out entirely. |
| `epc_cache` | Wall type, insulation, glazing, heating, build year, SAP score, per property, from the EPC register. |
| `postcode_cache` | Saved copy of a finished report, so repeat lookups don't redo the work. |
| `leads` | Email, postcode, saved report, consent flags. |

Flood risk and live flood warnings are checked live against the government's own system, not stored in our own table.

## Thresholds: green / orange / red

| Metric | Green | Orange | Red |
|---|---|---|---|
| Water hardness (mg/L) | Under 120 | 120-250 | Over 250 |
| Nitrate (mg/L) | Under 25 | 25-50 | Over 50 (legal limit) |
| Lead (µg/L) | Under 5 | 5-10 | Over 10 (legal limit) |
| THMs (µg/L) | Under 50 | 50-100 | Over 100 |
| Chlorine (mg/L) | Under 0.5 | 0.5-1.0 | Over 1.0 |
| pH | 7.0-8.5 | Just outside that | Below 6.5 or above 9.5 |
| Lead pipe risk (build year) | 1970 or later | 1940-1970 | Before 1940 |
| PM2.5 (µg/m3) | 5 or under | 5-10 | Over 10 |
| NO2 (µg/m3) | 10 or under | 10-40 | Over 40 (legal limit) |
| Radon class | 1-2 | 3-4 | 5-6 |
| Distance to major road | Over 200m | 50-200m | Under 50m |
| EPC/SAP band | C or above | D-E | F-G |
| Road noise at night | 40dB or under | 40-45dB | Over 45dB |
| Rail noise at night | 40dB or under | 40-44dB | Over 44dB |
| Flood risk | Very Low/Low | Medium | High |
| Historic landfill | Not within 250m | -- | Within 250m |
| Green space nearby | Within 300m | 300-800m | None within 800m |

## Our own composite scores (not official measurements)

**Damp & Mould risk** -- sum points from these five checks:

| Check | 0 pts | 1 pt | 2 pts |
|---|---|---|---|
| Wall type | Cavity, insulated | Cavity uninsulated / solid insulated | Solid, uninsulated |
| Windows | Double/triple glazed | -- | Single glazed |
| Ventilation | Mechanical system | Extractor fans | None/natural only |
| Heating fuel | Electric | Gas | -- |
| Built | 1919 or later | Before 1919 | -- |

Total 0-8. Green 0-2, Orange 3-5, Red 6-8.

**Overheating risk** -- sum points from these three checks:

| Check | 0 pts | 1 pt | 2 pts |
|---|---|---|---|
| Local density (tercile) | Bottom third nationally | Middle third | Top third |
| Ventilation (same field as above) | Mechanical | Extractor fans | None |
| Top floor flat | No | Yes | -- |

Total 0-5. Green 0-1, Orange 2-3, Red 4-5.

## Live vs. batch-built data

**Checked live, every request:** exact location, EPC (fallback), flood risk, current flood warnings, air quality problem area status.

**Built once, then looked up:** water company data, geology hardness model, air pollution, radon, noise, light pollution, green space, historic landfill.

**Cut, not included:** industrial pollution sources, aircraft noise, ground stability/subsidence data.

